{# Sent by SN_SexualHistory.dll when an OStim or SexLab scene ends, once for everyone who took part, the player included.
   The answer becomes that participant's SkyrimNet memory of the scene.
   Context: owner_name, owner_form_id, framework, location, game_date, real_minutes,
   participants (list of {name, form_id, is_player, is_owner, memories}), scene_details (list),
   climaxes (list of names), events_before (the last events before the scene) and events (those
   recorded while it ran), each a list of "Name -> Target (type): text", oldest first. #}
You are an expert on the Elder Scrolls universe, especially Skyrim. Your task is to turn a sexual encounter into a coherent first-person memory for a character within the game, true to what the encounter really was for them.

{{ render_template("submodules\\system_head\\0010_setting") }}

Generate a first-person memory for {{ owner_name }} of the sexual encounter described below.

## You
{{ render_character_profile("full", formid_to_uuid(owner_form_id)) }}

## First, judge what this encounter was
Before writing, work out from everything given what kind of encounter this was for {{ owner_name }}:
- the events before the scene (how it came about: an invitation, a seduction, a price agreed, an order, a threat, a dare, a celebration...);
- the events and lines during it, and the OStimNet intent when the scene details give one;
- the participants' relationship, character profiles and memories of each other (spouses, lovers, strangers, client and worker, master and servant, captor and captive...);
- the place (a home, an inn, a brothel, a camp...) and any money, favour or deal involved;
- whether it was forceful or one-sided.
Then place it plainly: loving, between partners who care for each other; a casual or curious fling; a paid job or other transaction; a duty or an obligation; reluctant; or forced. Sex is not affection: unless the context shows love or warmth, do not invent any. A worker with a client may feel only professional distance, boredom or relief that it is over; someone pressured or forced feels nothing like tenderness. When the context is unclear, keep the feelings modest rather than romantic.

## Instructions
Write the memory from {{ owner_name }}'s perspective:
1. Write in first person, as a recollection (no "last week" etc.).
2. Say plainly what kind of encounter it was (for example "a paying customer", "my wife", "a stranger I barely knew"), who took part, where, and what happened between them, using their names.
3. Say how {{ owner_name }} felt during and after it, and how the others seemed to feel, judging from what they said and did. The feelings must fit the kind of encounter you judged above, {{ owner_name }}'s personality and how they already feel about the others.
4. Mention what was said or done around the encounter when it matters (how it began, payment, promises, quarrels, what came after).
5. Use only what is given. Do not invent events, lines, feelings or relationships.
6. Be frank but not graphic: name what happened plainly, without lurid detail.
7. 3-6 dense sentences. Use concrete, searchable terms (names, places, actions).
8. Write in the same language as the character profile and the events.

## Response Format
Respond ONLY with a JSON object:
{% raw %}
```json
{
  "content": "First-person memory, 3-6 sentences: what kind of encounter it was, who, where, what happened, how I and the others felt.",
  "emotion": "joyful|content|neutral|indifferent|bored|uneasy|ashamed|concerned|fearful|angry|disgusted|surprised|sad|traumatized",
  "importance_score": 0.8-1.0,
  "tags": ["name", "location", "kind of encounter", "action", "theme"],
  "type": "RELATIONSHIP|JOY|TRAUMA|EXPERIENCE"
}
```
{% endraw %}

- emotion: the one that fits the kind of encounter; "joyful" or "content" only when the context shows it was welcome.
- type: RELATIONSHIP when it changed or confirmed a bond between people who matter to each other, JOY when it was mainly a happy experience, TRAUMA when it was forced or distressing for {{ owner_name }}, EXPERIENCE otherwise (a transaction, a duty or a casual encounter is usually EXPERIENCE).
- importance_score: between 0.8 and 1.0; such an encounter is never a minor memory. 0.95-1.0 for a first time, a forced encounter, or one that changes a relationship; 0.85-0.9 for a meaningful one; 0.8 for a routine one, including routine work.
- tags: 5-10 lower-case tags (names, place, the kind of encounter such as "romance", "casual", "paid", "duty", "forced", acts, themes).

[ user ]
Memory owner: {{ owner_name }}
Location: {{ location }}
In-game time: {{ game_date }}
Duration (real time): about {{ real_minutes }} minutes

Participants:
{% for p in participants %}- {{ p.name }}{% if p.is_owner %} (THIS IS YOU){% endif %}{% if p.is_player %} (the player){% endif %}: {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", formid_to_uuid(p.form_id)) }}
{% if length(p.memories) > 0 %}    Relevant memories of {{ p.name }}:
{% for m in p.memories %}    - {{ m }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
What the scene showed ({{ framework }}), in order:
{% if length(scene_details) == 0 %}- (no details recorded)
{% else %}{% for d in scene_details %}- {{ d }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if length(climaxes) > 0 %}Climaxes: {% for c in climaxes %}{{ c }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
Events just before the scene (oldest first):
{% if length(events_before) == 0 %}- (none recorded)
{% else %}{% for e in events_before %}- {{ e }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
Events recorded during the scene (oldest first):
{% if length(events) == 0 %}- (none)
{% else %}{% for e in events %}- {{ e }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
